Aim
To write a Python program to implement various list operations.
Algorithm
Start the program.
Create a list num = [50, 30, 20, 40, 60, 20].
Display the length of the list.
Append an element to the list and display it.
Insert an element at a specific position and display it.
Remove an element from the list and display it.
Remove the last element using pop() and display it.
Count occurrences of an element in the list.
Find the index of an element.
Sort the list and display it.
Reverse the list and display it.
Copy the list and display it.
Extend the list with another list and display it.
Find maximum value in the list.
Find minimum value in the list.
Find sum of all elements in the list.
Clear the list and display it.
Stop the program.

CODE

num = [50, 30, 20, 40, 60, 20]

print("the length of the array is :", len(num))

# append
num.append(10)
print("the element added is:", num)

# insert
num.insert(2, 90)
print("after insertion:", num)

# remove
num.remove(30)
print("after remove():", num)

# pop
num.pop()
print("after pop():", num)

# count
print("after count:", num.count(20))

# index
x = num.index(90)
print("after index():", x)

# sort
num.sort()
print("after sorting:", num)

# reverse
num.reverse()
print("after reverse:", num)

# copy
new_list = num.copy()
print("after copying:", new_list)

# extend
num.extend([15, 5])
print("after extending:", num)

# max
print("after max:", max(num))

# min
print("after min:", min(num))

# sum
print("after sum:", sum(num))

# clear
num.clear()
print("after clear():", num)

